{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1308694-thallain-questions-beasties-and-lurks","id":1308694,"title":"Thallain Questions: Beasties and Lurks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-29T08:45:17-07:00","id":1308694,"title":"Thallain Questions: Beasties and Lurks","content":"A number of the Thallain in C20 lack any real description of their Birthrights. As follows:<br /> <br /> Beasties<br /> What does the Beastie Form actually do? Are their stats or benefits? Claws, bite etc? I am thinking that while in this Beastie form the fae gains two additional dice for Physical Attributes, but the creature\u2019s Appearance drops to 0. What do you think?<br /> <br /> Lurks<br /> Omnivorous Hunger is pretty vague. Is this the same as the Redcap Dark Hunger? Or are they just immune to ingested poisons? If its just a tendency to eat garbage then they are woefully underbalanced.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-29-2019, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:13:33-07:00","id":1308815,"title":"","content":"Beasties animal form works the same as the Pooka one except the animal they change into doesn\u2019t need to be real. That is to say they gain animal stats according to their form. Scaled wolf with horns would use basic wolf stats with added attack option of ramming with it\u2019s horns and depending if the scales are just visual or not, ST/player decision, they could give a dot of soak or just be there for the disturbing look, or perhaps give the wolf a grapple attack option if the scales represent it\u2019s serpentlike ability to contort itself around it\u2019s prey. So basically, sadly, it\u2019s pretty much ST call. This is actually one of those things I originally really hoped would have been fixed in C20 as Beasties have had this problem since their first appearance.<br /> <br /> Lurks Endowment actually works as it says on the tin, they can eat anything they can for into their mouths. It\u2019s currently balanced against Dark Appetite by not having any Glamour costs associated with it while also not giving a direct attack options. Note that Dark Appetite requires a Glamour expenditure to allow eating of tough or toxic materials while Omnivorous Hunger is always free. If it fits in your mouth you can eat it, no matter what it is.<br /> <br /> Or that\u2019s how I interpret them until we get a Book Of Thallain, wishful thinking I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Typos 04-29-2019, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T06:53:19-07:00","id":1308920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1308694-thallain-questions-beasties-and-lurks?p=1308815#post1308815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasties animal form works the same as the Pooka one except the animal they change into doesn\u2019t need to be real. That is to say they gain animal stats according to their form. Scaled wolf with horns would use basic wolf stats with added attack option of ramming with it\u2019s horns and depending if the scales are just visual or not, ST/player decision, they could give a dot of soak or just be there for the disturbing look, or perhaps give the wolf a grapple attack option if the scales represent it\u2019s serpentlike ability to contort itself around it\u2019s prey. So basically, sadly, it\u2019s pretty much ST call. This is actually one of those things I originally really hoped would have been fixed in C20 as Beasties have had this problem since their first appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also had hoped for some clarity on the matter. So while I will award creative ideas from players, I think I will use the following rules for Beastie Form below. This is the same as the Protean power Form of the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Beastie Form:</b> When completely alone, Beasties may shapeshift into a monstrous beast (or back) over one turn. It costs one point of Glamour to change into Beastie form, though it is free to return to mortal seeming. While in the Beastie Form, the changeling can use any Art he possesses. Furthermore, each form gives the character the abilities of that creature. While in Beastie Form the changeling has no hands and cannot speak but has teeth and claws inflict Strength + 1 lethal damage. It can run at double speed, and the difficulties of all Perception rolls are reduced by two. <br /> <br /> As Beasties are likely to get into fights in their critter form, I thought this needed clarifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1308694-thallain-questions-beasties-and-lurks?p=1308815#post1308815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lurks Endowment actually works as it says on the tin, they can eat anything they can for into their mouths. It\u2019s currently balanced against Dark Appetite by not having any Glamour costs associated with it while also not giving a direct attack options. Note that Dark Appetite requires a Glamour expenditure to allow eating of tough or toxic materials while Omnivorous Hunger is always free. If it fits in your mouth you can eat it, no matter what it is.<br /> <br /> Or that\u2019s how I interpret them until we get a Book Of Thallain, wishful thinking I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that. It is the equivalent of the level one Bone Gnawer gift &quot;Cooking&quot; in that is allows sustenance from garbage. Though I might ask for a Wits+Survival roll (diff 6) to make a meal if it is something truly vile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 04-30-2019, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:35:40-07:00","id":1309037,"title":"","content":"@MythAdvocate<br /> Lurkers Omnivorous Hunger is both more and less than the Cooking Gift. More in that it allows the Lurker to eat whatever s/he can fit into her/his mouth, need to get rid of something quickly like a small knife or some evidence if it fits into your mouth your golden just eat it. Less in that it wont allow one to feed others. But the point is Lurkers can eat anything not limited to garbage, living, dead, edible or not if the Lurker can fit it through it\u2019s mouth it can eat it. No roll, no cost. It looses to a Redcaps Dark Appetite in that Lurkers dont have the Bite of a Redcap and thus no bite attack to rip limbs and such and the mouth of a Lurker is decidedly smaller than that of a Redcap but the Omnivorous Hunger is free of cost which balances it out. And unlike Cooking it takes absolutely no prep time.<br /> <br /> Just my personal take on the matter, naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:46:45-07:00","id":1309039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1308694-thallain-questions-beasties-and-lurks?p=1309037#post1309037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@MythAdvocate<br /> Lurkers Omnivorous Hunger is both more and less than the Cooking Gift. More in that it allows the Lurker to eat whatever s/he can fit into her/his mouth, need to get rid of something quickly like a small knife or some evidence if it fits into your mouth your golden just eat it. Less in that it wont allow one to feed others. But the point is Lurkers can eat anything not limited to garbage, living, dead, edible or not if the Lurker can fit it through it\u2019s mouth it can eat it. No roll, no cost. It looses to a Redcaps Dark Appetite in that Lurkers dont have the Bite of a Redcap and thus no bite attack to rip limbs and such and the mouth of a Lurker is decidedly smaller than that of a Redcap but the Omnivorous Hunger is free of cost which balances it out. And unlike Cooking it takes absolutely no prep time.<br /> <br /> Just my personal take on the matter, naturally YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I get it. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T16:13:04-07:00","id":1314603,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time, someone came up with an idea for Beastie form.<br /> Every Beastie gets an &quot;animal affinity&quot; just like the pooka, except their animals have weird features. Green fur, horns, tentacles, scary voices, whatever. <br /> However, these features were only aesthetic... unless you bought them in XP. They were bought as if they were Redes, and they would cost 2 XP per Chimera Point cost... Of course, the ST would have to limit which ones he would allow in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T21:16:04-07:00","id":1315079,"title":"","content":"Here's the really short <a href=\"https://www.digitaldreaming.org/righttodream/rules-beastieform.html\" target=\"_blank\">Beastie Form </a>fan idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T22:28:43-07:00","id":1315806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1308694-thallain-questions-beasties-and-lurks?p=1315079#post1315079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the really short <a href=\"https://www.digitaldreaming.org/righttodream/rules-beastieform.html\" target=\"_blank\">Beastie Form </a>fan idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup that's the rule I use, though I'm thinking of giving them flat out ten Glamour points or something instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}